{"author":{"id":"31c1b62b11a393a3d65ff9d58a47851781880bb7c306667336048a53227ddd9a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1702902349,"nonce":"mYE6qJfsc9ORO9Xwvzm1G7XBSIU=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOCGKeh85u4tMF","github-url":"https://github.com/git-bug/git-bug/issues/572#issuecomment-1860358917"},"message":"Hi,\nI am reopening the issue, since I am having the same with the version 0.8.0 of git-bug.\nTo me, it looks like the ssh config file is ignored:\n\n```\n$ git bug pull\n13:16:57.712053 git.c:748               trace: exec: git-bug pull\n13:16:57.712081 run-command.c:661       trace: run_command: git-bug pull\nFetching remote ...\nError: unknown error: 13:16:57.734930 git.c:462               trace: built-in: git upload-pack mysite:myproject\n\n```\n\n`mysite` is defined in `~/.ssh/config`\n\nAs a workaround, one should defined the ssh connection without any config alias, and also the **absolute path** for `myproject` (couldn't get relative path to work):\n```\ncat .git/config\n[remote \"origin\"]\nssh://git@myipordomain:22222/home/git/myproject\nfetch = +refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/*\n```\nBy doing this, I am finally able to `git bug pull/push`.\nTo me, it looks like it's a golang problem, but I don't have any knowledge in that language.","files":null},{"type":6,"timestamp":1702902610,"nonce":"L+1gEKMJ09MiVcjpq7LDyDHUIYk=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lALOCGKeh85u4tMFzjzOrTM"},"target":"48233e90e17799ddba7598ba8901aa4f507e9a7d0eacd8521f615609e63485d1","message":"Hi,\nI am reopening the issue, since I am having the same with the version 0.8.0 of git-bug.\nTo me, it looks like the ssh config file is ignored:\n\n```\n$ git bug pull\n13:16:57.712053 git.c:748               trace: exec: git-bug pull\n13:16:57.712081 run-command.c:661       trace: run_command: git-bug pull\nFetching remote ...\nError: unknown error: 13:16:57.734930 git.c:462               trace: built-in: git upload-pack mysite:myproject\n\n```\n\n`mysite` is defined in `~/.ssh/config`\n\nAs a workaround, one should defined the ssh connection without any config alias, and also the **absolute path** for `myproject` (couldn't get relative path to work):\n```\ncat .git/config\n[remote \"origin\"]\nssh://git@myipordomain:22222/home/git/myproject\nfetch = +refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/*\n```\nYou also might what to `ssh-add ~/.ssh/yourkey`, which totally makes no sense to me. I hate agents and I don't get why it's needed here.\n\nBy doing all of this, I am finally able to `git bug pull/push`. \nTo me, it looks like it's a golang problem, but I don't have any knowledge in that language.","files":null},{"type":6,"timestamp":1702902657,"nonce":"1SlKURmd3m0SKnKjCV10cd+CLjc=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lALOCGKeh85u4tMFzjzOsIg"},"target":"48233e90e17799ddba7598ba8901aa4f507e9a7d0eacd8521f615609e63485d1","message":"Hi,\nI am reopening the issue, since I am having the same with the version 0.8.0 of git-bug.\nTo me, it looks like the ssh config file is ignored:\n\n```\n$ git bug pull\n13:16:57.712053 git.c:748               trace: exec: git-bug pull\n13:16:57.712081 run-command.c:661       trace: run_command: git-bug pull\nFetching remote ...\nError: unknown error: 13:16:57.734930 git.c:462               trace: built-in: git upload-pack mysite:myproject\n\n```\n\n`mysite` is defined in `~/.ssh/config`\n\nAs a workaround, one should defined the ssh connection without any config alias, and also the **absolute path** for `myproject` (couldn't get relative path to work):\n```\ncat .git/config\n[remote \"origin\"]\nssh://git@myipordomain:22222/home/git/myproject\nfetch = +refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/*\n```\nYou also might what to `ssh-add ~/.ssh/yourkey`, which totally makes no sense to me. From a security perspective, I really hate agents and I don't get why it's needed here.\n\nBy doing all of this, I am finally able to `git bug pull/push`. \nTo me, it looks like it's a golang problem, but I don't have any knowledge in that language.","files":null},{"type":6,"timestamp":1702903840,"nonce":"VgvrV70nJK6Y84vbZxQ+Q3nvqy0=","metadata":{"github-id":"UCE_lALOCGKeh85u4tMFzjzPAhk"},"target":"48233e90e17799ddba7598ba8901aa4f507e9a7d0eacd8521f615609e63485d1","message":"Hi,\nI am reopening the issue, since I am having the same with the version 0.8.0 of git-bug binary (linux x86_64).\nTo me, it looks like the ssh config file is ignored:\n\n```\n$ git bug pull\n13:16:57.712053 git.c:748               trace: exec: git-bug pull\n13:16:57.712081 run-command.c:661       trace: run_command: git-bug pull\nFetching remote ...\nError: unknown error: 13:16:57.734930 git.c:462               trace: built-in: git upload-pack mysite:myproject\n\n```\n\n`mysite` is defined in `~/.ssh/config`\n\nAs a workaround, one should defined the ssh connection without any config alias, and also the **absolute path** for `myproject` (couldn't get relative path to work):\n```\ncat .git/config\n[remote \"origin\"]\nssh://git@myipordomain:22222/home/git/myproject\nfetch = +refs/heads/*:refs/remotes/origin/*\n```\nYou also might what to `ssh-add ~/.ssh/yourkey`, which totally makes no sense to me. From a security perspective, I really hate agents and I don't get why it's needed here.\n\nBy doing all of this, I am finally able to `git bug pull/push`. \nTo me, it looks like it's a golang problem, but I don't have any knowledge in that language.","files":null}]}